{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/d375-measure/packet-v4-1.md'","aggregated_output":"# Packet v4-1\n\n**The question:** How much data-center segment revenue will Nvidia report for FY2027?\n\nDue 2027-02-28. Possible answers:\n- 1 Strongly bullish: FY2027 data-center segment revenue is at least $450 billion.\n- 2 Bullish: FY2027 data-center segment revenue is at least $400 billion but below $450 billion.\n- 3 Neutral: FY2027 data-center segment revenue is at least $350 billion but below $400 billion.\n- 4 Bearish: FY2027 data-center segment revenue is at least $300 billion but below $350 billion.\n- 5 Strongly bearish: FY2027 data-center segment revenue is below $300 billion.\n\n**40 statements read on 2026-09-22:**\n\n- **v4-1-1** (stored attribution: Sea): Sea plans to adopt Nvidia's Vera Rubin platform across Shopee, Monee and Garena to build and deploy AI models and agents at greater scale.\n  - Passage: \"Singapore-founded Sea will adopt Nvidia's Vera Rubin platform to build and deploy artificial-intelligence (AI) models and agents at greater scale across its Shopee, Monee and Garena businesses.\"\n- **v4-1-2** (stored attribution: barchart.com (analyst)): The author estimates roughly 25% of Nvidia's FY2028 revenue, potentially $175 billion, will come from customers receiving company-backed financing funded off Nvidia's balance sheet.\n  - Passage: \"Nvidia is financing a growing share of its sales to AI startups, with roughly 25% of fiscal 2028 revenue expected to come from customers receiving some form of company-backed financing — potentially $175 billion funded off its own balance sheet.\"\n- **v4-1-3** (stored attribution: TweakTown): TweakTown reported that US third-party RTX 5070 card prices had risen from around $650 a couple of months earlier to around $850, attributing the increase to the RAM crisis.\n  - Passage: \"I expect the RTX 5070 PCs will last longer - they're both still in stock at the time of writing - but even these represent a decent bargain given that you're looking at around $850 for a third-party card in the US these days. That's up from around $650 just a couple of months ago, and GPU pricing is getting a whole lot worse thanks to the RAM crisis.\"\n- **v4-1-4** (stored attribution: MarketBeat author): MarketBeat estimated that NVIDIA revenue grew more than 80% over the past year.\n  - Passage: \"NVIDIA may have smaller share-price gains lately, but its business is growing at a blistering pace, with revenue expanding more than 80% over the past year versus Apple's far more reserved 14%.\"\n- **v4-1-5** (stored attribution: NCS): NCS is developing physical-AI applications for humanoid robotics.\n  - Passage: \"NCS is also developing physical-AI applications for humanoid robotics.\"\n- **v4-1-6** (stored attribution: Jensen Huang): Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang projected that chip sales could double in calendar 2027.\n  - Passage: \"CEO Jensen Huang has projected that chip sales could double in calendar year 2027\"\n- **v4-1-7** (stored attribution: Alibaba Group Holding Limited): Alibaba said it plans to expand global data-center capacity above 20 gigawatts by 2032.\n  - Passage: \"Alibaba Group Holding Limited (NYSE: BABA ) also discussed future Qwen models scaling to 5 trillion to 10 trillion parameters and its plans to expand global data-center capacity above 20 gigawatts by 2032.\"\n- **v4-1-8** (stored attribution: The Information): The Information reported on September 16, 2026, that Apple was developing enterprise AI inference servers using two or four M8 Ultra chips, potentially launching in 2029, and had considered Nvidia's NVLink Fusion to connect them; the project and Nvidia's involvement were not finalized.\n  - Passage: \"The Information reported on September 16 that Apple Inc. (NASDAQ: AAPL ) is developing enterprise servers around future M8 Ultra processors. Designs under consideration use either two or four M8 Ultra chips, with a possible 2029 launch aimed primarily at AI inference. Apple has also considered NVIDIA Corporation's (NASDAQ: NVDA ) NVLink Fusion technology to connect those processors.\"\n- **v4-1-9** (stored attribution: David Russell, TradeStation): TradeStation's David Russell said Nvidia customers Meta and Alphabet have moved to design AI chips internally, a shift he believes will gradually erode Nvidia's pricing power and market share.\n  - Passage: \"David Russell, global head of market strategy at TradeStation, pointed to the growing threat of customers building their own silicon, noting that Meta $META Platforms and Alphabet $GOOGL are among the major Nvidia buyers that have moved to design AI chips internally — a shift he believes will gradually erode Nvidia's pricing power and market share.\"\n- **v4-1-10** (stored attribution: NVIDIA): NVIDIA said its technical partnership with The Coalition enables GeForce RTX features—including DLSS Super Resolution, Dynamic Multi Frame Generation, Reflex and ray tracing—in Gears of War: E-Day.\n  - Passage: \"Thanks to a technical partnership with Gears of War: E-Day developer The Coalition, GeForce RTX gamers can activate a suite of features to accelerate and further enhance Gears of War: E-Day, delivering the definitive PC experience:\nDLSS Super Resolution and Dynamic Multi Frame Generation will multiply frame rates, whilst simultaneously increasing image quality.\nNVIDIA Reflex will reduce PC latency, making gameplay even more responsive, and possibly giving you a competitive edge in Versus.\nAnd the Ray Tracing cores found in all GeForce RTX GPUs will accelerate the rendering of Unreal Engine 5.8’s Lumen and MegaLights ray tracing technologies.\"\n- **v4-1-11** (stored attribution: Nvidia management): Nvidia management guided for third-quarter revenue of approximately $108 billion, implying 89% year-over-year growth.\n  - Passage: \"management has guided for approximately $108 billion in third-quarter revenue, implying 89% growth.\"\n- **v4-1-12** (stored attribution: NVIDIA): NVIDIA released Isaac ROS 5.0, a new collection of GPU-accelerated packages for the Robot Operating System, on 2026-09-22.\n  - Passage: \"NVIDIA Corp. today released Isaac ROS 5.0, its latest collection of GPU-accelerated packages built on the Robot Operating System open framework.\"\n- **v4-1-13** (stored attribution: barchart.com (analyst)): The author reports that 45 of 50 analysts rate Nvidia a Strong Buy and that the mean price target is about $326, implying 42% upside.\n  - Passage: \"Analysts remain overwhelmingly bullish, with 45 of 50 firms rating the stock a \"Strong Buy,\" a mean price target near $326 implying 42% upside from current levels\"\n- **v4-1-14** (stored attribution: Analysts compiled by Bloomberg): Bloomberg-compiled analyst estimates project Nvidia gross margin below 72% in FY2027's fourth quarter, after 75% last quarter, with a recovery expected afterward.\n  - Passage: \"Nvidia's gross margin came in at 75% last quarter but analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show it sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter.\"\n- **v4-1-15** (stored attribution: barchart.com (analyst)): The author calculates Nvidia trades at 14 times next-fiscal-year consensus earnings, versus its 10-year average P/E of 61, AMD's trailing P/E above 200, and Broadcom's P/E of 46.\n  - Passage: \"At 14 times next fiscal year's consensus earnings estimate, Nvidia trades at a fraction of its 10-year average price/earnings (P/E) ratio of 61 – and well below semiconductor peers like Advanced Micro Devices (AMD) at over 200 times trailing earnings and Broadcom (AVGO) at 46 times.\"\n- **v4-1-16** (stored attribution: NVIDIA): NVIDIA said it will deliver additional NVIDIA features in The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt — Remastered on September 29, 2026.\n  - Passage: \"And on September 29th, NVIDIA will be delivering even more cutting-edge features through Remastered.\"\n- **v4-1-17** (stored attribution: Colette Kress): Nvidia CFO Colette Kress guided for 70% revenue growth in FY2028, versus 45% previously modeled by Wall Street, according to the author.\n  - Passage: \"CFO Colette Kress guided for 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028 — a figure that far exceeded the 45% Wall Street had previously modeled.\"\n- **v4-1-18** (stored attribution: Delos Data): Delos Data announced on September 15, 2026, that it raised more than $100 million to develop networking chips and software for heterogeneous AI data centers; Playground Global joined the financing round.\n  - Passage: \"Delos Data announced on September 15 that it raised more than $100 million to develop networking chips and software for increasingly heterogeneous AI data centers. Playground Global, where Gelsinger is a general partner, joined the round.\"\n- **v4-1-19** (stored attribution: NCS): NCS adopted Nvidia Nemotron models and a video-search-and-summarisation blueprint for enterprise and public-sector work.\n  - Passage: \"For instance, NCS has adopted Nemotron models and its video-search-and-summarisation blueprint for enterprise and public-sector work.\"\n- **v4-1-20** (stored attribution: iApp Technology): Thailand's iApp Technology is adapting Nvidia Nemotron 3 Nano for Thai-language legal work.\n  - Passage: \"Meanwhile, Thailand's iApp Technology is adapting Nemotron 3 Nano for Thai-language legal work.\"\n- **v4-1-21** (stored attribution: Bloomberg): Bloomberg-reported estimates expect Nvidia revenue and net income each to grow roughly 90% or more in FY2027.\n  - Passage: \"Nvidia's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in its current fiscal year.\"\n- **v4-1-22** (stored attribution: The Information): The Information estimated that networking equipment represents 10% to 15% of AI data-center hardware costs, a potential revenue pool for Nvidia beyond GPUs.\n  - Passage: \"The Information reported that networking equipment can represent 10% to 15% of AI data-center hardware costs, giving Nvidia a meaningful revenue pool beyond GPUs.\"\n- **v4-1-23** (stored attribution: Nvidia): Nvidia reported fiscal second-quarter revenue of $96.2 billion, up more than 100% year over year, and data center revenue of $89 billion, up 117%.\n  - Passage: \"Fiscal second-quarter revenue more than doubled year over year to $96.2 billion, with data center revenue surging 117% to $89 billion\"\n- **v4-1-24** (stored attribution: Singapore's Home Team Science and Technology Agency (HTX)): Singapore's HTX is beginning research using two Nvidia Nemotron models for public-safety applications.\n  - Passage: \"Meanwhile, Singapore's Home Team Science and Technology Agency (HTX) is beginning research using two Nemotron models for public-safety applications.\"\n- **v4-1-25** (stored attribution: NVIDIA): NVIDIA said AION 2’s global release on September 30, 2026, will include DLSS 4.5 Super Resolution and Multi Frame Generation support for GeForce RTX GPUs.\n  - Passage: \"When the global version is released on September 30th, AION 2 will include support for DLSS 4.5 Super Resolution and Multi Frame Generation, enabling the highest levels of image quality and performance on all GeForce RTX GPUs.\"\n- **v4-1-26** (stored attribution: Pat Gelsinger): Pat Gelsinger said that compute left idle while waiting for data wastes money and energy.\n  - Passage: \"Gelsinger described idle compute waiting for data as a major waste of both money and energy.\"\n- **v4-1-27** (stored attribution: NVIDIA): NVIDIA contributed a standard data-handling interface to ROS 2 Lyrical for robotics software to work across computing hardware, including GPUs.\n  - Passage: \"NVIDIA contributed a standard data-handling interface to ROS 2 Lyrical that helps robotics software work efficiently across different computing hardware, including GPUs.\"\n- **v4-1-28** (stored attribution: VideoCardz): VideoCardz reported that Walmart sold more than 1,000 CyberPowerPC systems with RTX 5080 GPUs in one day before they sold out.\n  - Passage: \"According to VideoCardz, the cheaper RTX 5080 systems sold out in a day flat, with Walmart shifting over 1,000 units apparently.\"\n- **v4-1-29** (stored attribution: barchart.com (analyst)): The author says Nvidia has more than $100 billion in off-balance-sheet guarantees tied to projects including the SB Energy campus for OpenAI.\n  - Passage: \"off-balance-sheet guarantees exceeding $100 billion tied to projects like the SB Energy campus for OpenAI introduce credit risk that traditional valuation metrics do not capture.\"\n- **v4-1-30** (stored attribution: NVIDIA): NVIDIA said Remedy Entertainment’s CONTROL Resonant is scheduled to launch on September 24, 2026, with DLSS 4.5 and path tracing.\n  - Passage: \"Remedy Entertainment’s CONTROL Resonant is launching September 24th with DLSS 4.5 and path tracing.\"\n- **v4-1-31** (stored attribution: CyberPowerPC): CyberPowerPC began shipping prebuilt gaming PCs with NVIDIA GeForce RTX 50 Founders Edition GPUs for sale through Walmart during its September 21–27, 2026 GeForce Week promotion.\n  - Passage: \"CyberPowerPC is now shipping prebuilt gaming PCs with NVIDIA’s own GeForce RTX 50 Founders Edition graphics cards. The systems are being sold through Walmart as part of the retailer’s GeForce Week promotion, which runs from September 21 through September 27.\"\n- **v4-1-32** (stored attribution: Zacks analyst): Zacks says China remains largely closed to data-center compute and NVIDIA is taking on larger supply commitments, customer credit support and long-dated guarantees.\n  - Passage: \"China remains largely closed to data center compute, and NVIDIA is taking on larger supply commitments, customer credit support and long-dated guarantees.\"\n- **v4-1-33** (stored attribution: videocardz.com): Videocardz.com reported that a CyberPowerPC system with an RTX 5080 Founders Edition, priced at $2,299, sold out in one day after receiving more than 1,000 orders; the period was one day, with no specific date given.\n  - Passage: \"I think the $2,299 system that sold out in one day with over 1,000 orders makes sense given how much RTX 5080 cards cost now.\"\n- **v4-1-34** (stored attribution: barchart.com (analyst)): The author reports that analyst EPS estimates for Nvidia FY2029 rose from $8.50 to $15.68 over nine months.\n  - Passage: \"earnings estimates that have been revised sharply higher — from $8.50 to $15.68 per share for fiscal 2029 — over just the past nine months.\"\n- **v4-1-35** (stored attribution: Viettel AI): Viettel AI fine-tuned Nvidia Nemotron 3 Super for Vietnamese-language and agentic applications, and plans to use it in Legal AI for Viettel employees and external customers.\n  - Passage: \"In Vietnam, Viettel AI has fine-tuned Nemotron 3 Super for Vietnamese-language and agentic applications. The model is set to be used in Legal AI, an agent system for Viettel Group employees and external customers.\"\n- **v4-1-36** (stored attribution: barchart.com (analyst)): The author estimates Nvidia trades below 17 times forward 12-month earnings, its lowest multiple in over a decade and about half its early-2025 multiple.\n  - Passage: \"Nvidia (NVDA) stock is currently trading at less than 17 times expected forward 12-month earnings, representing the cheapest valuation the shares have commanded in over a decade and roughly half the multiple investors were willing to pay as recently as early 2025.\"\n- **v4-1-37** (stored attribution: barchart.com (analyst)): The author calculates that Nvidia shares would roughly double over 12 to 18 months if the trailing P/E stays at 28 and consensus earnings projections are met.\n  - Passage: \"If Nvidia simply maintains its current trailing P/E of 28 while delivering on consensus earnings projections, the stock would roughly double over the next 12 to 18 months.\"\n- **v4-1-38** (stored attribution: ST Engineering): ST Engineering is using Nvidia NeMo tools and cuOpt software to develop its AI Studio platform and deploy applications, including for marine maintenance, repair and overhaul.\n  - Passage: \"At ST Engineering, Nvidia's NeMo tools and cuOpt software are being used to develop its AI Studio platform and deploy AI applications in areas including marine maintenance, repair and overhaul.\"\n- **v4-1-39** (stored attribution: Delos Data): Delos is designing a network intended to work across different types of compute hardware, rather than only NVIDIA accelerators.\n  - Passage: \"Reuters reported that Delos is designing the network to work across different types of compute hardware rather than assuming every accelerator comes from NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ: NVDA ).\"\n- **v4-1-40** (stored attribution: AI Singapore): AI Singapore is adding Nvidia Nemotron open models and NeMo tools to its SEA-LION model family.\n  - Passage: \"This includes AI Singapore adding Nemotron open models and NeMo tools to SEA-LION, its model family for Southeast Asian languages and cultures.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"item\":\"v4-1-1\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The adoption plan gives no purchase amount or timing for FY2027.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-2\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The estimate concerns FY2028 revenue, not FY2027 data-center revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-3\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"RTX gaming-card prices do not establish data-center revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-4\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Past growth in total revenue does not specify FY2027 data-center revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-5\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The robotics work gives no Nvidia data-center revenue or purchase expectation.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-6\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The projection is for chip sales in calendar 2027, mostly after FY2027.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-7\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Alibaba's 2032 capacity plan does not specify Nvidia purchases in FY2027.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-8\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The potential server launch is in 2029 and Nvidia's involvement is undecided.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-9\",\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"Customers designing their own AI chips could reduce Nvidia's data-center sales or pricing.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-10\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The partnership concerns gaming features rather than data-center revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-11\",\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"The FY2027 third-quarter total revenue guidance constrains how much data-center revenue that quarter can contribute.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-12\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The robotics software release gives no FY2027 data-center revenue expectation.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-13\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Stock ratings and price targets do not state data-center revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-14\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Gross margin is a profitability measure rather than data-center revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-15\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Earnings multiples do not determine FY2027 data-center revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-16\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The game features concern gaming products rather than data-center revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-17\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The growth guidance concerns total revenue in FY2028.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-18\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The startup's fundraising does not establish its effect on Nvidia's FY2027 sales.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-19\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The software adoption gives no purchase amount or timing for FY2027.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-20\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The model adaptation gives no FY2027 data-center purchase or revenue figure.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-21\",\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"Expected FY2027 total revenue growth informs the overall revenue available to the data-center segment.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-22\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The industry hardware-cost share does not specify Nvidia's FY2027 networking sales.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-23\",\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"The $89 billion in second-quarter data-center revenue contributes directly to the FY2027 total.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-24\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The research use of models gives no FY2027 data-center purchase or revenue figure.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-25\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The game features concern GeForce products rather than data-center revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-26\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The general cost of idle compute does not establish Nvidia's FY2027 revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-27\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The robotics software interface gives no FY2027 data-center revenue expectation.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-28\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Gaming PC sales do not establish data-center segment revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-29\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The guarantees describe credit exposure without an FY2027 data-center sales figure or timing.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-30\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The game launch concerns gaming features rather than data-center revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-31\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The promotion concerns gaming PCs rather than data-center sales.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-32\",\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"China's limited access to data-center compute constrains a potential market for Nvidia's FY2027 sales.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-33\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Sales of a gaming PC do not establish data-center segment revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-34\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The earnings estimates concern FY2029 rather than FY2027 data-center revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-35\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The model deployment gives no FY2027 data-center purchase or revenue figure.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-36\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The stock's earnings multiple does not determine data-center revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-37\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The share-price calculation does not specify FY2027 data-center revenue.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-38\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The software use gives no FY2027 data-center purchase or revenue figure.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-39\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The network design does not establish a change in Nvidia's FY2027 sales.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v4-1-40\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The model and tool adoption gives no FY2027 data-center purchase or revenue figure.\"}\n{\"done\":true,\"items\":40}"}}
